rd", "insufficient_funds", "insufficient_available_balance", "declined", "merchant_request", "payment_disputed", "payment_refund_failed", "payment_refund_not_attempted", "refund_failed". object.idempotency_key (Optional): string. The caller's Idempotency-Key when this refund was created, including refunds created by issuing a credit note. Use GET /v1/refunds?idempotency_key= to recover a lost response. object.initiated_by (Required): string. Who decided to make this refund: `merchant` for you or your integration, `flint` for a refund Flint made on its own to return a payment it couldn't accept. Unlike a Return's `initiated_by`, it doesn't say which credential asked. Read-only. Value enum: "merchant", "flint". object.invoice_id (Optional): string. ID of the invoice whose credit note this refund paid out. Present only on refunds issued through a credit note. Example: "inv_01KEZF7C00A5GEBMWHEAJFSAR4". object.line_item_allocations (Optional): Array of {@see RefundLineItemAllocationInput}. How the refund applied to each order line item it covered, with quantity, tax, and adjustments. object.line_item_allocations[] (Value): {@see RefundLineItemAllocationInput}. How a refund applied to one order line item: quantity, refunded amount, tax, adjustments, and modifier allocations. object.merchant_id (Required): string. ID of the merchant this resource belongs to. Example: "mer_01KEZF7C00KPYH1DDFPCCX3B6E". object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Stored caller-owned key-value data. See `MetadataInput` for key, value, and size rules. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.order (Optional): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `order`; `null` when expanded and there is no related order. object.order.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see