EF6". object.pending_reason (Required): string or null. Why a pending refund is waiting. `null` when `status` isn't `pending`, or when the refund is on its way without review. Value enum: "manual_review", null. object.processed_by (Required): string. Who moved or is moving the money for this refund. Flint processes refunds through a processor or a gift card; merchant means the merchant returned the money outside Flint and recorded it here. Existing refunds are processed by Flint. Value enum: "flint", "merchant". object.reason (Required): string or null. Why the refund was issued. It never changes how the money moves. The buyer's refund receipt shows it only for `requested_by_customer`, `duplicate`, `defective_product`, `wrong_item_shipped`, `never_received`, `not_as_described`, `arrived_too_late`, `accidental_order`, and `out_of_stock`. Only Flint sets `payment_returned`, and it can't be sent in requests. `null` when no reason was recorded. Value enum: "duplicate", "fraudulent", "requested_by_customer", "defective_product", "wrong_item_shipped", "never_received", "not_as_described", "arrived_too_late", "customer_changed_mind", "better_price_found", "accidental_order", "other", "out_of_stock", "payment_returned", null. object.reason_message (Optional): string. Note explaining the refund, up to 1,024 characters. object.refund_id (Required): string. Unique identifier for this refund, prefixed `ref_`. Example: "ref_01KEZF7C003DTD59WKYHEXYQ1K". object.refund_platform_fee (Required): boolean. Whether the request asked to return the platform fee on the payments this refund refunds (refund_platform_fee). Each payment refund's refunded_platform_fee_money is what it returns. object.refund_reference (Optional): string. The merchant's opaque check, wire, or other reference for money returned outside Flint, preserved exactly. Present only when processed_by is merchant and a reference was supplied. external_reference_id is the merchant's own refund ID. minLength: 1. maxLength: 25