nds (Optional): Array of {@see RefundTaxBreakdownRefundInput}. Tax reversed on order-level charges and flat taxes, one entry per tax breakdown. Tax reversed on line items is in `line_item_allocations[].tax_breakdown_refunds`. object.tax_breakdown_refunds[] (Value): {@see RefundTaxBreakdownRefundInput}. The tax refunded for one tax breakdown on an order. object.tender_allocations (Optional): Array of {@see RefundTenderAllocationInput}. Every tender the refund drew from, payment or gift card, with its amount, tip share, status, and destination. object.tender_allocations[] (Value): {@see RefundTenderAllocationInput}. One tender's share of a refund, listed in the refund's tender allocations. object.unissued_gift_card_recoveries (Optional): Array of {@see RefundUnissuedGiftCardRecoveryInput}. Cash returned after an unissued gift card purchase refund failed. Return it through a new refund against payment_intent_id and order_line_item_id. It does not issue another card. Source remaining and pending amounts describe the entire original settlement allocation; repeated entries for that source are not additive. object.unissued_gift_card_recoveries[] (Value): {@see RefundUnissuedGiftCardRecoveryInput}. Details of a gift card purchase refunded before the card was issued, including the amounts recovered. object.updated_at (Required): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.version (Required): integer. Persisted version of this resource's owned state. Expanded resources and external observations can change independently. Format: uint64. minimum: 1. previous_attributes (Optional): object. Previous values of changed top-level fields in data.object, at this delivery's API version. Nested changes include the whole previous top-level value. A value is null when the field was absent before the change. Omitted when Flint did not record the previous state, including synthetic test events.
